IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 6 Division 2, sections 205A to 205D -- the exemptions from the audit. LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- s 205A: a company exempt from audit requirements is exempt from section 205(1) and (2); s 205B: a dormant company; s 205C: a small company
-- (the meaning of "small company" and "small group" is the Thirteenth Schedule's, sgc2-sch13-small.l4: this module takes "the company is a small
-- company" and "the company is part of a small group" as plain facts, which the seat computes from the Schedule); s 205D: the Registrar may
-- require audited statements despite the exemption.
-- The seam to s 7A(2) (sg-solvency.l4) is the last function of the first section below: the company is exempt under section 205B or 205C.

§ `The seam to section 7A(2): exempt under section 205B or 205C`

-- Plain BOOLEAN seam: s 7A(2) of the keel takes "the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C" as a fact. The two answers are
-- ss 205B(1) and (7) and s 205C(1) and (2). Section 205C(1) answers NOTHING for a company that is not small (a scope limit, fork line F-S4), and this plain BOOLEAN
-- turns any answer that is not JUST TRUE, NOTHING included, into FALSE, because s 7A(2) takes a plain BOOLEAN. Read FALSE here as "not shown exempt under
-- section 205B or 205C", never as "the text says the company is not exempt".
GIVEN `the answer under section 205B` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 205C` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205B and 205C the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` MEANS
    (`the answer under section 205B` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer under section 205C` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

§ `Sections 205A to 205D: the acts and parties of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 205A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 205A(2) appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company`
    `s 205B(4)(d) accompany the annual return with a statement by the directors`
    `s 205C(7) attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return lodged under section 197`
    `s 205D lodge the audited financial statements and the auditor's report the Registrar's notice requires`

§ `Section 205A: companies exempt from the obligation to appoint auditors`

-- src:19529 | 205A.—(1) Despite section 205, a company which is exempt from
-- src:19530 | audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, and its directors, are
-- src:19531 | exempt from section 205(1) or (2), as the case may be.
@ref s 205A(1) (src:19529-19531)
GIVEN `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205A(1) the company and its directors are exempt from section 205(1) or (2)` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company which is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, and its directors, are exempt from section 205(1) or (2)" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)): it says nothing of a company that is not so exempt, which section 205 itself answers (fork line F-S4)

-- (2): where a company ceases to be exempt, it must appoint a person or persons as auditor at any time before the next annual general meeting.
-- "before the next annual general meeting": the last day is the day before the meeting (fork line F-P4). The text says "a person or persons", where s 205(1) says "an accounting entity"
-- (finding in NOTES.md): only an accounting entity may act as auditor (s 10 of the keel).
-- src:19536 | (2) Where a company ceases to be so exempt, the company must
-- src:19537 | appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company
-- src:19538 | at any time before the next annual general meeting; and the auditors
-- src:19539 | so appointed hold office until the conclusion of that meeting.
@ref s 205A(2) (src:19536-19539)
GIVEN `the day of the next annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205A(2) the last day for the company to appoint an auditor` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the next annual general meeting` 1 Days

@ref s 205A(2) (src:19536-19539)
GIVEN `the company has ceased to be exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the next annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the company has appointed a person or persons to be auditor or auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company made the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205A(2) the company is in default of the duty to appoint an auditor` MEANS
    IF     `the company has ceased to be exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the company has appointed a person or persons to be auditor or auditors`
              `the day the company made the appointment`
              (`s 205A(2) the last day for the company to appoint an auditor` `the day of the next annual general meeting`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company ceases to be so exempt, the company must appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company at any time before the next annual general meeting" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or no cessation: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205A(2) (src:19536-19539)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the company ceased to be exempt` IS A DATE
      `the day of the next annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205A act`
`s 205A(2) the company must appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205A(2) appoint a person or persons to be auditor or auditors of the company`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the company ceased to be exempt` (`s 205A(2) the last day for the company to appoint an auditor` `the day of the next annual general meeting`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not appoint an auditor before the next annual general meeting after it ceased to be exempt from audit requirements"

-- "and the auditors so appointed hold office until the conclusion of that meeting": an "until" bar.
@ref s 205A(2) (src:19536-19539)
GIVEN `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205A(2) the auditors appointed hold office` MEANS
    IF `the next annual general meeting of the company has concluded`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the auditors so appointed hold office until the conclusion of that meeting" (an "until" bar)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:19541 | (3) If default is made in complying with subsection (2), the
-- src:19542 | company and every director of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:19543 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:19544 | exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 205A(3) (src:19541-19544)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 205(17) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and every director of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" names the persons it makes guilty (split site (i), fork line F-E1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (2)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 205A(3) (src:19541-19544)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 205A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 205A(3) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with section 205A(2)` person EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 205B: the dormant company`

-- One transaction of the company: whether its record must be kept under section 199(1) (s 205B(8)), and which of the matters in s 205B(3) it arises from.
DECLARE `s 205B(3) transaction` HAS
    `s 205B(8) its record is required to be kept under section 199(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(a) it arises from the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the constitution pursuant to an undertaking of the subscriber in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(b) it arises from the appointment of a secretary of the company under section 171` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(c) it arises from the appointment of an auditor under section 205` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(d) it arises from the maintenance of a registered office under sections 142, 143 and 144` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(e) it arises from the keeping of registers and books under sections 88, 131, 173, 189 and 191` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(f) it arises from the payment of a fee or charge (including a fee, penalty or interest for late payment) payable under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(fa) it arises from the payment of a composition amount payable under section 409B or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(fb) it is the payment or receipt by the company of a nominal sum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 205B(3)(fb) the nominal sum, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 205B(3)(fb) the most that may be prescribed as such a nominal sum, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 205B(3)(g) it arises from another matter that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:19548 | 205B.—(1) A company is exempt from audit requirements if —
-- src:19550 | (a) it has been dormant from the time of its formation; or
-- src:19552 | (b) it has been dormant since the end of the previous financial
-- src:19553 | year.
@ref s 205B(1) (src:19548-19553)
GIVEN `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` MEANS
    IF `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` OR `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is exempt from audit requirements if -- (a) it has been dormant from the time of its formation; or (b) it has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year" (an "if" gate; a failed "if" counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

-- (8): "accounting transaction" means a transaction the accounting or other record of which is required to be kept under section 199(1): a closed "means".
-- src:19646 | (8) In this section, “accounting transaction” means a transaction the
-- src:19647 | accounting or other record of which is required to be kept under
-- src:19648 | section 199(1).
@ref s 205B(8) (src:19646-19648)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 205B(3) transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(8) "accounting transaction" the transaction is an accounting transaction` MEANS
    IF transaction's `s 205B(8) its record is required to be kept under section 199(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'accounting transaction' means a transaction the accounting or other record of which is required to be kept under section 199(1)" (a "means" definition)

-- (3): transactions arising from any of (a) to (g) "are to be disregarded". A list not closed with "only": a transaction that arises from none of them is not said to be disregarded.
-- (fb): a nominal sum "not exceeding such amount as may be prescribed": the amount is left to regulations and is supplied.
-- src:19559 | (3) For the purpose of subsection (2), transactions of a company
-- src:19560 | arising from any of the following are to be disregarded:
-- src:19562 | (a) the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the
-- src:19563 | constitution pursuant to an undertaking of the subscriber in
-- src:19564 | the constitution;
-- src:19566 | (b) the appointment of a secretary of the company under
-- src:19567 | section 171;
-- src:19569 | (c) the appointment of an auditor under section 205;
-- src:19571 | (d) the maintenance of a registered office under sections 142,
-- src:19572 | 143 and 144;
-- src:19574 | (e) the keeping of registers and books under sections 88, 131,
-- src:19575 | 173, 189 and 191;
-- src:19577 | (f) the payment of any fee or charge (including any fee,
-- src:19578 | penalty or interest for late payment) payable under any
-- src:19579 | written law;
-- src:19584 | (fa) the payment of any composition amount payable under
-- src:19585 | section 409B or any other written law;
-- src:19587 | (fb) the payment or receipt by the company of such nominal
-- src:19588 | sum not exceeding such amount as may be prescribed;
-- src:19590 | (g) such other matter as may be prescribed.
@ref s 205B(3) (src:19559-19590)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 205B(3) transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205B(3) helper: the transaction arises from a listed matter` MEANS
       transaction's `s 205B(3)(a) it arises from the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the constitution pursuant to an undertaking of the subscriber in the constitution`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(b) it arises from the appointment of a secretary of the company under section 171`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(c) it arises from the appointment of an auditor under section 205`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(d) it arises from the maintenance of a registered office under sections 142, 143 and 144`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(e) it arises from the keeping of registers and books under sections 88, 131, 173, 189 and 191`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(f) it arises from the payment of a fee or charge (including a fee, penalty or interest for late payment) payable under a written law`
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(fa) it arises from the payment of a composition amount payable under section 409B or any other written law`
    OR (    transaction's `s 205B(3)(fb) it is the payment or receipt by the company of a nominal sum`
        AND transaction's `s 205B(3)(fb) the nominal sum, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST transaction's `s 205B(3)(fb) the most that may be prescribed as such a nominal sum, in Singapore dollars`)
    OR transaction's `s 205B(3)(g) it arises from another matter that may be prescribed`

@ref s 205B(3) (src:19559-19590)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 205B(3) transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(3) the transaction is to be disregarded` MEANS
    IF `s 205B(3) helper: the transaction arises from a listed matter` transaction
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "transactions of a company arising from any of the following are to be disregarded" lists matters without "only", and says nothing of a transaction arising from none of them

-- (2): "A company is dormant during a period in which no accounting transaction occurs": a transaction counts if it is an accounting transaction and is not disregarded under (3).
-- src:19555 | (2) A company is dormant during a period in which no accounting
-- src:19556 | transaction occurs; and the company ceases to be dormant on the
-- src:19557 | occurrence of such a transaction.
@ref s 205B(2) (src:19555-19557)
GIVEN transactions IS A LIST OF `s 205B(3) transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(2) the company is dormant during the period` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN t YIELD (t's `s 205B(8) its record is required to be kept under section 199(1)`) AND (NOT (`s 205B(3) helper: the transaction arises from a listed matter` t))) transactions
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is dormant during a period in which no accounting transaction occurs" (an accounting transaction that subsection (3) does not disregard occurred in the period)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 205B(2) (src:19555-19557)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 205B(3) transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(2) the company ceases to be dormant on the transaction` MEANS
    IF transaction's `s 205B(8) its record is required to be kept under section 199(1)` AND (NOT (`s 205B(3) helper: the transaction arises from a listed matter` transaction))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company ceases to be dormant on the occurrence of such a transaction" (a transaction that is not an accounting transaction, or that subsection (3) disregards, is not "such a transaction")

-- (4): "Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)" -- (a) the copies of the financial statements ... to be sent under section 203
-- need not be audited; (b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to the auditor's report or a copy of the report; (c) copies of an auditor's report need not be laid before the
-- company in a general meeting; (d) the annual return must be accompanied by a statement by the directors. Each is gated by a "where": a failed "where" is JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-W1).
-- src:19594 | (4) Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt from
-- src:19595 | audit requirements under subsection (1) —
-- src:19597 | (a) the copies of the financial statements or consolidated
-- src:19598 | financial statements and balance sheet of the company to
-- src:19599 | be sent under section 203 need not be audited;
@ref s 205B(4)(a) (src:19594-19599)
GIVEN `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(4)(a) the copies of the financial statements to be sent under section 203 need not be audited` MEANS
    IF `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1) -- (a) the copies of the financial statements ... to be sent under section 203 need not be audited" (a "where" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-W1)

-- src:19601 | (b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to
-- src:19602 | the auditor’s report or a copy of the report;
@ref s 205B(4)(b) (src:19601-19602)
GIVEN `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(4)(b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to the auditor's report or a copy of it` MEANS
    IF `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt ... -- (b) section 203 has effect with the omission of any reference to the auditor's report or a copy of the report" (a "where" gate: fork line F-W1)

-- src:19604 | (c) copies of an auditor’s report need not be laid before the
-- src:19605 | company in a general meeting; and
@ref s 205B(4)(c) (src:19604-19605)
GIVEN `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(4)(c) copies of an auditor's report need not be laid before the company in a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt ... -- (c) copies of an auditor's report need not be laid before the company in a general meeting" (a "where" gate: fork line F-W1)

-- src:19607 | (d) the annual return of the company to be lodged with the
-- src:19608 | Registrar must be accompanied by a statement by the
-- src:19609 | directors —
-- src:19611 | (i) that the company is a company referred to in
-- src:19612 | subsection (1)(a) or (b) as at the end of the
-- src:19613 | financial year;
-- src:19615 | (ii) that no notice has been received under subsection (6)
-- src:19616 | in relation to that financial year; and
-- src:19618 | (iii) as to whether the accounting and other records
-- src:19619 | required by this Act to be kept by the company have
-- src:19620 | been kept in accordance with section 199.
@ref s 205B(4)(d) (src:19607-19620)
GIVEN `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the annual return is accompanied by a statement by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that the company is a company referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b) as at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (6) in relation to that financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(4)(d) the directors are in default of the duty to accompany the annual return with the statement` MEANS
    IF     `the company is, at the end of the financial year, exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)`
       AND (NOT (    `the annual return is accompanied by a statement by the directors`
                 AND `the statement says that the company is a company referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b) as at the end of the financial year`
                 AND `the statement says that no notice has been received under subsection (6) in relation to that financial year`
                 AND `the statement says whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company have been kept in accordance with section 199`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is, at the end of a financial year, exempt ... -- (d) the annual return of the company to be lodged with the Registrar must be accompanied by a statement by the directors (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) as to whether the accounting and other records ... have been kept in accordance with section 199" (a duty met, or no exemption: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- No time limit is stated here (the return's own deadline is section 197, which is outside these ranges) and no consequence: no breach path.
@ref s 205B(4)(d) (src:19607-19620)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205A act`
`s 205B(4)(d) the directors must accompany the annual return with a statement` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 205B(4)(d) accompany the annual return with a statement by the directors`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not accompany the annual return of the exempt company with the statement section 205B(4)(d) requires"

-- (5): where a company exempt under (1) ceases to be dormant it thereupon ceases to be exempt; it remains exempt in relation to accounts for the financial year in which it was dormant throughout.
-- src:19624 | (5) Where a company which is exempt from audit requirements
-- src:19625 | under subsection (1) ceases to be dormant, it thereupon ceases to be
-- src:19626 | so exempt; but it remains so exempt in relation to accounts for the
-- src:19627 | financial year in which it was dormant throughout.
@ref s 205B(5) (src:19624-19627)
GIVEN `the company is exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be dormant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(5) the company ceases to be exempt from audit requirements` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` AND `the company ceases to be dormant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company which is exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1) ceases to be dormant, it thereupon ceases to be so exempt" (a "where" gate: fork line F-W1)

@ref s 205B(5) (src:19624-19627)
GIVEN `the company was dormant throughout the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceased to be dormant during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(5) the company remains exempt in relation to the accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the company was dormant throughout the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the company ceased to be dormant during the financial year`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it thereupon ceases to be so exempt; but it remains so exempt in relation to accounts for the financial year in which it was dormant throughout" -- the exception saves only a year in which the company was dormant throughout, and a year in which it ceased to be dormant is not one; added after the independent review, assumed, not ruled (fork line F-W1)
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a company that ceases to be dormant; a year in which the company neither was dormant throughout nor ceased to be dormant is outside it (whether the company is exempt then is for subsection (1))

-- (6): "Any member or members holding not less than 5% of the total number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares) or any class of those shares (excluding treasury shares), or not less
-- than 5% of the total number of members of the company (excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member) may, by written notice to the company during a financial year but not later
-- than one month before the end of that year, require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for that year." "5%": held times 20 is at least the total, and the members "holding" must hold something (a limb whose holders hold none is not met).
-- The time limit is a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-P1). The holding and "written notice" are named complements of the
-- grant: NOTHING where they are not met (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1).
-- src:19629 | (6) Any member or members holding not less than 5% of the total
-- src:19630 | number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares)
-- src:19631 | or any class of those shares (excluding treasury shares), or not less
-- src:19636 | than 5% of the total number of members of the company (excluding
-- src:19637 | the company itself if it is registered as a member) may, by written
-- src:19638 | notice to the company during a financial year but not later than
-- src:19639 | one month before the end of that year, require the company to obtain
-- src:19640 | an audit of its accounts for that year.
@ref s 205B(6) (src:19629-19640)
GIVEN `the number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares held by the members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares of the class concerned, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the class shares held by the members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members who gave the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(6) the members may require the company to obtain an audit of its accounts for the year` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the day the notice was given` AT LEAST `the first day of the financial year`
            AND `the day the notice was given` AT MOST (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the last day of the financial year` 1 Months))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by written notice to the company during a financial year but not later than one month before the end of that year" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-P1)
    ELSE (IF     `the notice was in writing`
             AND (    (`the number of those shares held by the members who gave the notice` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of those shares held by the members who gave the notice` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares`)
                  OR (`the number of the class shares held by the members who gave the notice` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of the class shares held by the members who gave the notice` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the number of issued shares of the class concerned, excluding treasury shares`)
                  OR (`the number of members who gave the notice` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of members who gave the notice` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the number of members of the company, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member`))
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for members holding "not less than 5%" of the shares, of a class, or of the members, "by written notice"; the subsection does not say that a smaller holder, or a notice not in writing, has no effect (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1)

-- (7): "Where a notice is given under subsection (6), the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year to which the notice relates."
-- The function is named for the bar the text states ("is not entitled"), so that JUST TRUE reads as the text does: the exemption is taken away. Its gate is a "where": when no notice has been given the
-- answer is JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-W1), which says only that this subsection takes nothing away. An "entitled"-named function the Guide does not settle
-- (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3): counted in fork line F-N1 with the other reading, NOTHING.
-- src:19642 | (7) Where a notice is given under subsection (6), the company is not
-- src:19643 | entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the
-- src:19644 | financial year to which the notice relates.
@ref s 205B(7) (src:19642-19644)
GIVEN `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(7) the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the flat negative of the text, in its own words: "the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year to which the notice relates"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice is given under subsection (6), ..." (a "where" gate failed: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); an "entitled"-named function: fork lines F-W1 and F-N1)

-- The answer under section 205B for a financial year: the exemption of (1), unless a notice under (6) has been given (7).
@ref s 205B(7) (src:19642-19644)
GIVEN `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205B(1) and (7) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `s 205B(7) the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` `a notice has been given under subsection (6) in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year to which the notice relates"
    ELSE `s 205B(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements` `the company has been dormant from the time of its formation` `the company has been dormant since the end of the previous financial year`

§ `Section 205C: the small company`

-- (1): "Subject to subsections (3), (4) and (6), a company that is a small company in respect of a financial year is exempt from audit requirements for that financial year."
-- A company that is not a small company is not said by this subsection to be non-exempt (a dormant company is exempt under section 205B, for one): a scope limit with no "only",
-- so NOTHING (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); fork line F-S4). The three "subject to" limbs are the functions that follow.
-- src:19652 | 205C.—(1) Subject to subsections (3), (4) and (6), a company that
-- src:19653 | is a small company in respect of a financial year is exempt from audit
-- src:19654 | requirements for that financial year.
@ref s 205C(1) (src:19652-19654)
GIVEN `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is part of a small group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `s 205C(6) this section applies to the company for the financial year` `the first day of the financial year` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a company with respect to its financial statements for a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015" (subsection (6): a flat negative)
    ELSE (IF `s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` `the company is a parent company` `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` `the company is part of a small group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a parent company unless the parent company (a) is a small company; and (b) is part of a small group" (subsection (3): an "unless" not met)
          ELSE (IF `s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` `the company is a subsidiary company` `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` `the company is part of a small group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a subsidiary company unless the subsidiary company (a) is a small company; and (b) is part of a small group" (subsection (4): an "unless" not met)
                ELSE (IF `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company that is a small company in respect of a financial year is exempt" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)); it says nothing of a company that is not a small company (fork line F-S4)

-- (2): section 205B(4), (6) and (7) apply, with the necessary modifications, to a small company so exempt. The same functions answer: `s 205B(4)(a)` to `(d)` and `s 205B(6)`.
-- The bar of section 205B(7), applied to a small company, is the second function here.
-- src:19658 | (2) Section 205B(4), (6) and (7) applies, with the necessary
-- src:19659 | modifications, to a small company so exempt.
@ref s 205C(2) (src:19658-19659)
GIVEN `the small company is exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(2) section 205B(4), (6) and (7) apply to the small company` MEANS
    IF `the small company is exempt from audit requirements under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 205B(4), (6) and (7) applies, with the necessary modifications, to a small company so exempt" speaks of a company that is exempt under subsection (1) and says nothing of another

@ref s 205C(2) (src:19658-19659)
GIVEN `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(2) the small company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the flat negative of section 205B(7), in its own words, as subsection (2) applies it: "the company is not entitled to the exemption ... in respect of the financial year to which the notice relates"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice is given under subsection (6), ..." (section 205B(7), applied to a small company by section 205C(2): a "where" gate failed, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); an "entitled"-named function: fork lines F-W1 and F-N1)

-- The answer under section 205C for a financial year: the exemption of (1), unless a notice under section 205B(6), as (2) applies it, has been given.
@ref s 205C(2) (src:19658-19659)
GIVEN `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is part of a small group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(1) and (2) the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205C for the financial year` MEANS
    IF     (`s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` `the company is a parent company` `the company is a subsidiary company` `the company is part of a small group` `the first day of the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 205C(2) the small company is not entitled to the exemption under subsection (1) in respect of the financial year` `a notice has been given under section 205B(6) as subsection (2) applies it, in relation to the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is not entitled to the exemption ... in respect of the financial year to which the notice relates" (section 205B(7), applied by section 205C(2))
    ELSE `s 205C(1) the company is exempt from audit requirements for the financial year` `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` `the company is a parent company` `the company is a subsidiary company` `the company is part of a small group` `the first day of the financial year`

-- src:19663 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a parent company unless the
-- src:19664 | parent company —
-- src:19666 | (a) is a small company; and
-- src:19668 | (b) is part of a small group.
@ref s 205C(3) (src:19663-19668)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is part of a small group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(3) subsection (1) applies to the company as a parent company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a parent company` AND (NOT (`the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` AND `the company is part of a small group`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a parent company unless the parent company (a) is a small company; and (b) is part of a small group" (an "unless" not met)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars subsection (1) for a parent company that is not both; once the "unless" is met it does not say that subsection (1) applies (subsection (1) answers; fork line F-U1)

-- src:19672 | (4) Subsection (1) does not apply to a subsidiary company unless
-- src:19673 | the subsidiary company —
-- src:19675 | (a) is a small company; and
-- src:19677 | (b) is part of a small group.
@ref s 205C(4) (src:19672-19677)
GIVEN `the company is a subsidiary company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is part of a small group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(4) subsection (1) applies to the company as a subsidiary company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a subsidiary company` AND (NOT (`the company is a small company in respect of the financial year` AND `the company is part of a small group`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a subsidiary company unless the subsidiary company (a) is a small company; and (b) is part of a small group" (an "unless" not met)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as for subsection (3) (fork line F-U1)

-- (5): "In this section, 'small company' and 'small group' have the meanings given in the Thirteenth Schedule." The two answers are the Schedule's (sgc2-sch13-small.l4); when no head of the Schedule holds,
-- the Schedule answers JUST FALSE (the delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)) and this section takes it as "not a small company". NOTHING never reaches here.
-- src:19681 | (5) In this section, “small company” and “small group” have the
-- src:19682 | meanings given in the Thirteenth Schedule.
@ref s 205C(5) (src:19681-19682)
GIVEN `the answer of the Thirteenth Schedule for the company and the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205C(5) "small company" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` MEANS
    `the answer of the Thirteenth Schedule for the company and the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE

@ref s 205C(5) (src:19681-19682)
GIVEN `the answer of the Thirteenth Schedule for the group and the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205C(5) "small group" has the meaning given in the Thirteenth Schedule` MEANS
    `the answer of the Thirteenth Schedule for the group and the financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (6): "This section does not apply to a company with respect to its financial statements for a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015".
-- src:19686 | (6) This section does not apply to a company with respect to its
-- src:19687 | financial statements for a financial year commencing before 1 July
-- src:19692 | 2015 and such a company must prepare its accounts or consolidated
-- src:19693 | accounts and its directors must lay them at its annual general meeting
-- src:19694 | in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date.
@ref s 205C(6) (src:19686-19694)
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(6) this section applies to the company for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the financial year` LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2015)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a company with respect to its financial statements for a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (6) says nothing of a financial year that commences on or after 1 July 2015 (subsection (1) answers)

-- (6), second limb: such a company "must prepare its accounts or consolidated accounts and its directors must lay them at its annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date".
-- Part VI as it then stood is not among the sources: whether the company did so is a supplied fact.
@ref s 205C(6) (src:19686-19694)
GIVEN `the company's financial year commenced before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company prepared its accounts or consolidated accounts in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors laid them at the annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(6) the company and its directors are in default of the duty to prepare and lay the accounts as the earlier Part VI required` MEANS
    IF `the company's financial year commenced before 1 July 2015` AND (NOT (`the company prepared its accounts or consolidated accounts in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date` AND `the directors laid them at the annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such a company must prepare its accounts or consolidated accounts and its directors must lay them at its annual general meeting in accordance with Part VI in force immediately before that date" (a duty met, or not a financial year commencing before 1 July 2015: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- src:19698 | (7) Without limiting section 197(2), a company mentioned in
-- src:19699 | subsection (6) must, when lodging a return with the Registrar under
-- src:19700 | section 197, attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so
-- src:19701 | prepared.
@ref s 205C(7) (src:19698-19701)
GIVEN `the company is a company mentioned in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged a return with the Registrar under section 197` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company attached a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205C(7) the company is in default of the duty to attach a copy of the accounts to the return` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company mentioned in subsection (6)` AND `the company has lodged a return with the Registrar under section 197` AND (NOT `the company attached a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so prepared`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company mentioned in subsection (6) must, when lodging a return with the Registrar under section 197, attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts so prepared" (a duty met, or no return lodged yet: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- No time limit of its own (the return's deadline is section 197, outside these ranges): no breach path.
@ref s 205C(7) (src:19698-19701)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205A act`
`s 205C(7) the company must attach a copy of the accounts to the return` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205C(7) attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return lodged under section 197`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not attach a copy of the accounts or consolidated accounts to the return it lodged under section 197"

§ `Section 205D: the Registrar may require an exempt company to lodge audited financial statements`

-- "Despite sections 205B and 205C, the Registrar may, if he or she is satisfied that there has been a breach of any provision of section 199 or 201 or that it is otherwise in the public interest to do so,
-- by written notice to a company exempt under either of those sections, require that company to lodge ... (a) its financial statements duly audited ...; and (b) an auditor's report mentioned in section 207".
-- A "may" whose "if" gate failed: NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12; fork line F-G1). What it means to the person: an exempt company can be made to lodge audited statements.
-- src:19708 | 205D. Despite sections 205B and 205C, the Registrar may, if he or
-- src:19709 | she is satisfied that there has been a breach of any provision of
-- src:19710 | section 199 or 201 or that it is otherwise in the public interest to do so,
-- src:19711 | by written notice to a company exempt under either of those sections,
-- src:19712 | require that company to lodge with the Registrar, within such time as
-- src:19713 | may be specified in that notice —
-- src:19715 | (a) its financial statements duly audited by the auditor or
-- src:19716 | auditors of the company or, where none has been
-- src:19717 | appointed, an auditor or auditors to be appointed by the
-- src:19718 | directors of the company for this purpose; and
-- src:19720 | (b) an auditor’s report mentioned in section 207 in relation to
-- src:19721 | those financial statements prepared by the auditor or
-- src:19722 | auditors of the company.
@ref s 205D (src:19708-19722)
GIVEN `the company is exempt under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that there has been a breach of a provision of section 199 or 201` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it is otherwise in the public interest to require the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205D the Registrar may require the exempt company to lodge audited financial statements` MEANS
    IF     `the company is exempt under section 205B or 205C`
       AND (`the Registrar is satisfied that there has been a breach of a provision of section 199 or 201` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it is otherwise in the public interest to require the lodgment`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may, if he or she is satisfied that there has been a breach of any provision of section 199 or 201 or that it is otherwise in the public interest to do so, by written notice to a company exempt under either of those sections, require" (a "may" whose "if" gate failed: the grant rule of 2026-11-12)

-- The company's side: once the notice is given, the company must lodge, within the time the notice specifies, (a) its financial statements duly audited and (b) an auditor's report mentioned in section 207.
-- The time is "such time as may be specified in that notice": the last day is the day the notice names (an input).
@ref s 205D (src:19708-19722)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the company a written notice under section 205D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the notice specifies for lodging` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged its financial statements duly audited and an auditor's report mentioned in section 207 in relation to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company lodged them` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205D the company is in default of the requirement in the Registrar's notice` MEANS
    IF     `the Registrar has given the company a written notice under section 205D`
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the company has lodged its financial statements duly audited and an auditor's report mentioned in section 207 in relation to them`
              `the day the company lodged them`
              `the last day the notice specifies for lodging`
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "require that company to lodge with the Registrar, within such time as may be specified in that notice -- (a) its financial statements duly audited ...; and (b) an auditor's report mentioned in section 207" (a requirement met in time, or not yet due, or no notice given: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 205D (src:19708-19722)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the Registrar gave the notice` IS A DATE
      `the last day the notice specifies for lodging` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 205A act`
`s 205D the company must lodge what the Registrar's notice requires` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 205D lodge the audited financial statements and the auditor's report the Registrar's notice requires`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the Registrar gave the notice` `the last day the notice specifies for lodging`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the audited financial statements and the auditor's report within the time the Registrar's notice specified"
